# defineProps types

Declare a named `interface` before passing it to `defineProps` or `withDefaults(defineProps<...>())`.

Name it `Props` or `<Component>Props`.

Always assign the macro result to `const props`.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
interface ButtonProps {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'ghost'
  type?: 'button' | 'submit' | 'reset'
}

const props = withDefaults(defineProps<ButtonProps>(), {
  variant: 'primary',
  type: 'button',
})
</script>
```

```ts
// ❌ inline
const props = defineProps<{
  variant?: 'primary'
}>()
```
